Spec: ServiceInitFromScript

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  Seed a `ServiceInstance`'s freshly created vitals from an existing restic backup during the
    very first install: render the packaged `init_job.yaml` template into a per-instance init
    Job (a restore Pod running `agent service restore` inside the instance namespace, plus its
    ServiceAccount, RoleBinding and optional scripts ConfigMap), apply the documents, and block
    until the Job finishes — all inside the `init_from::run(instance, context)` call made by
    ./install.rhai's first-install gate (`status.vitals` set + `status.tag` unset +
    `spec.initFrom` set). The file itself touches no restic and reads none of the three routing
    fields (source path, snapshot, Secret): @bctx::run(instance, context, `true`) copies them
    verbatim into the rendered pod env (`RESTIC_SNAPSHOT`, `SUB_PATH`, `envs_from` Secret), and
    the resolved restore semantics — latest-vs-id snapshot use, engine re-seeds, maintenance
    pair — live in the dispatched Pod's ./restore.sdd lane, not here. Byte-identical twin of
    ./../tenant/init_from.rhai; unlike ./backup.sdd and ./restore.sdd (Pod-side, CR-blind,
    exit-4/5 throw-only), this is the CR-side stage: it owns @set_status_init_failed and
    re-throws into the install lane's exit-1.

Exposes:
  @run(@instance, @context) — the module's sole @fn and entry point (`init_from.rhai` + `run`
    match the entry-point patterns of /agent/src/linting/rhai_checker.sdd); reached ONLY through
    @import_run("init_from", instance, context) from ./install.rhai — no Rust lane names the
    module, and the caller discards the return value whole (./install.sdd). A package
    `scripts/init_from.rhai` shadowing the name replaces this whole lane on that install.

Accepts:
  @instance — the injected @ServiceInstance @Dynamic. Direct reads in this file:
    `.metadata.namespace` (Job probe and the apply-namespace argument) and the
    @set_status_init_failed method on failure. Everything else flows through collaborators on
    the same object: @bctx::run requires `.status.vitals` (array, unguarded), `.status.scalables`
    (guarded) and — via @use_init_from `true` — `spec.initFrom.secretName` / `.subPath` /
    `.snapshot` each `!= ()`-nullable; `initFrom.version` is read by nobody on this path.
  @context — the install-lane map (same object ./install.rhai threads to every bucket). Direct
    reads: `template_dir` (unguarded property-on-`()` if non-map — the Rust lane always injects
    it via ./context.rhai) and `package_dir` (the `${context.package_dir}/pods` gate). The whole
    map is also @bctx::run's data source and the Handlebars render data, so the shipped template
    reads `instance.appslug`, `instance.namespace`, `instance["package"].type`,
    `cluster.vynil_namespace`, `agent_image`, `volumes`/`mounts`/`envs`/`envs_from`/`files`/
    `has_files`/`service_account` from it — that key contract is owned by
    ./../lib/build_context.sdd + ./context_service.rhai (pending) and ./../lib/backup_context.sdd
    respectively. Note the map's `instance` key (built view) is NOT the injected CR: templates
    read the key, @bctx::run's CR scans read the argument.
  Hooks — three optional @import_run module names: `init_from_pre`, `init_from_prepare`,
    `init_from_post`, each called with the same (instance, context) pair. None ships in any
    engine directory (./, ./../tenant, ./../lib) — package `scripts/` slots only.

Returns:
  The `context` map exactly as held after the try/catch, plus an `init_from_post` merge on a map
    return — a value ./install.rhai discards; the lane communicates only by side effects. The
    observable outcomes: the rendered documents applied through @dir::install_obj (shipped
    template yields ServiceAccount `{appslug}-backup`, RoleBinding `{appslug}-backup`, Job
    `{appslug}-init-restore` and — only when `has_files` — ConfigMap `{appslug}-backups-scripts`,
    all without their own `metadata.namespace` so all in `instance.metadata.namespace`), the
    full-filesystem restore landing inside the awaited Pod, and the `InitFrom` failure
    condition on error.

Raises:
  Zero error-fabricating @throw statement: the file's one throw is the bare `throw;` re-throw
    after the failure marker. @import_run swallows only the two skip markers
    (`No ${name} module, skipping.` and `No ${name}::run function, skipping.`), and only
    those — everything else propagates.
  Inside the @try (marker path): a raw raise from @bctx::run (dead/absent `status.vitals`,
    missing `instance` context key, the Cluster-branch Secrets @list_meta read — see its spec's
    Raises), from either @register_partial_dir call on a broken template, from
    @render_from and @yaml_decode_multi, the engine error of a non-map document reaching
    @dir::install_obj's `kind` dot, its `kind: ${obj.kind} is unknown from the apiServer.`
    throw, or a @wait::all timeout — becomes @set_status_init_failed(reason) (verbatim string;
    non-string through @json_encode) then `throw;`: the install lane continues to no later
    bucket and exits 1 (./install.sdd), with the condition `InitFrom`/`Warning` `InitFromFail`
    written (/common/src/instance_macros.sdd).
  Outside the @try: @set_status_init_failed's own KubeError replaces the original error; a
    raise inside the `init_from_pre` hook kills the lane with no marker at all; a raise inside
    the `init_from_post` hook (the only statement after the try) likewise leaves no marker even
    though apply+wait already succeeded (Tasks).
  The Job-probe inner @try/@catch warn-and-continue: any @k8s_resource, @exist or @list error is
    @log_warn'd (string verbatim, else @json_encode text) and the Job then rides the
    no-dedup apply path; @json_encode of an unserializable payload would re-raise out of that
    catch into the marker path (same open point as ./../lib/backup_context.sdd).

Handles:
  Stock image: all three hook names take the debug-log @import_run skip, the @type_of guard
    sees no map, and the lane runs on the unchanged `context`. A hook returning a non-map
    leaves the previous `context` in force (same merge discipline as ./install.sdd's buckets).
  Idempotent-Job gate: a rendered document whose `kind` is `"Job"` is applied only when no Job
    of that name currently exists in `instance.metadata.namespace` — probe
    `k8s_resource("Job", ns).@exist()` (true once the built-in kind resolved at construction,
    practically always; false silently skips the dedup), then `@list().items` filtered on
    `metadata.name`. A skipped Job is applied nowhere, waited on nowhere, and never logged.
  Documents of every other kind ride no probe: @dir::install_obj always re-applies them.
  Partial precedence: `template_dir` ships first, then `${package_dir}/pods` (only under
    @is_dir) registers second, so a package `pods/restore.yaml.hbs` / `pods/init_job.yaml.hbs`
    silently overwrites the shipped same-name partial.
  Failure text shape: the marker reason is the caught engine error's own text — no wrapper,
    no file/line prefix added at this level.

Must:
  Execute exactly: @import_run("init_from_pre") → map-merge guard → @try { @import_run
    ("init_from_prepare") + map-merge → @new_hbs + @register_partial_dir(`context.template_dir`)
    → conditional @register_partial_dir(`${context.package_dir}/pods`) → @yaml_decode_multi of
    @render_from(`"{{> init_job.yaml }}"`, @bctx::run(instance, context, `true`)) → per-document
    Job dedup gate → @dir::install_obj(obj, true, instance.metadata.namespace, false) for
    every applied document → @wait::all(applied_objs, `20*60`) } → on raise:
    @set_status_init_failed + `throw;` → @import_run("init_from_post") + map-merge → return
    `context`; nothing else, in no other order.
  Call @bctx::run with @use_init_from `true` — the ONLY site in the service tree that appends
    env `RESTIC_SNAPSHOT` (= `instance.spec.initFrom.snapshot`, possibly `()`-valued per
    ./../lib/backup_context.sdd) and the site that swaps `envs_from` to `initFrom.secretName`
    (default `backup-settings`), redirects `SUB_PATH` to `initFrom.subPath` (default
    `${namespace}/${appslug}` — so by default the instance restores its own backup path, and a
    different source instance is addressed purely through `subPath`), and withholds the
    per-Secret `/secrets/` mounts (secret values ride the initFrom Secret instead): this file
    passes all three fields through untouched.
  Keep the apply posture of `./../lib/install_from_dir.sdd`: single-object @install_obj per
    document in decoded-document order, `allow_cluster` `true` (no shipped init document is
    cluster-scoped; the flag is inert today), `force_ns` `false` (documents carry no
    `metadata.namespace`, so one namespace applies: `instance.metadata.namespace`), and NO
    bucket-ordering pass — the rendered stream needs no first/middle/last ordering.
  Await every applied object once, after the whole loop, through one @wait::all(applied_objs,
    `20*60`) call: ConfigMap/ServiceAccount/RoleBinding hit no lane's kind filter, the init Job
    gets `wait_done` 1200 s (contract in ./../lib/wait.sdd) — the whole restore must fit that
    budget or the lane fails via Raises.
  Write the failure marker with the two switched arms as written (string reason verbatim /
    other error `json_encode`d) and re-throw: success is never marked here — no
    `set_status_*` success call, condition or tag; the install close in ./install.sdd stamps
    `Ready`/`tag` later.
  Emit no @log_info, @log_debug or @log_error line at this level: the only logs are the two
    @log_warn shapes of the Job-probe catch (plus anything the imported collaborators log).
  Keep the import-time surface at the three top-level imports — `"backup_context"` as `bctx`,
    `"install_from_dir"` as `dir`, `"wait"` as `wait`, all side-effect-free per their specs —
    so module load touches no env, filesystem or cluster; a resolver miss is an eval error in
    the install lane before @run starts.
  Resolve every hook name against the four resolver directories frozen by the install Rust lane
    ({package_dir}/scripts first), so packages can ship the three hooks or shadow the whole lane.

Must not:
  Open or close a maintenance/scale window: no `maintenance_start`/`maintenance_stop`
    @import_run here (unlike ./backup.rhai and ./restore.sdd) — during the first install the
    scalables are not applied yet, and any workload quiescing is the restore Pod's own pair (a
    no-op TODO pair regardless, ./maintenance_start.rhai +
    ./maintenance_stop.rhai, specs pending).
  Read `spec.initFrom` (or `.status.vitals`) directly — the three routing fields reach the pod
    spec only via @bctx::run, so a second reader would fork the source-selection contract that
    ./../lib/backup_context.sdd owns.
  Wait on, re-apply or mark anything for the deduped existing Job — `to_apply` `false` means
    the object leaves no trace (Tasks records the decision open).

Depends on:
  ./../lib/backup_context.rhai — @run(..., `true`) half of the env/context contract (spec
    ./../lib/backup_context.sdd, which freezes this file as its @use_init_from `true` caller).
  ./../lib/install_from_dir.rhai — @install_obj single-object apply + applied-entry shape
    (./../lib/install_from_dir.sdd; the applied list here feeds no @remove/diff, only @wait).
  ./../lib/wait.rhai — @wait::all two-arg with the shared `20*60` budget (./../lib/wait.sdd).
  /agent/templates/init_job.yaml.hbs (+ nested /agent/templates/restore.yaml.hbs pod
    template) resolved through `context.template_dir` — the rendered shape itself is
    template-owned, not frozen here.
  wynil-core 0.7.7 engine API — @import_run shim, @new_hbs, @register_partial_dir, @render_from
    (partial-name = filename minus `.hbs`, silent same-name overwrite;
    /common/src/handlebarshandler.sdd), @is_dir, @yaml_decode_multi, @k8s_resource(kind, ns) +
    @exist, @list, @log_warn, @json_encode, @type_of.
  /common/src/instanceservice.sdd + /common/src/instance_macros.sdd — the
    @set_status_init_failed bridge and the `InitFrom`/`InitFromFail` condition it patches;
    /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — the @Script constructor mounting all of the above.

References:
  ./install.rhai + ./install.sdd — the sole caller: gate condition, (instance, context)
    injection and the returned-context discard frozen there; /agent/src/service/install.sdd —
    exit-1 lane every raise here lands in.
  ./../tenant/init_from.rhai — diff-verified byte-identical twin (unspecified).
  ./restore.sdd + ./backup.sdd — Pod-side siblings: ./restore.sdd is the lane the rendered
    Job dispatches and consumes the env of; both contrast CR-side marker posture with their
    CR-blind throw-only failure surfaces.
  /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs — nearest lane test file (Tasks).

Scenario: first install applies and awaits the init job
  Given the install gate true, a context whose `instance.appslug` is `shop`, no `pods/` dir and
    no existing `{appslug}-init-restore` Job
  When @run executes
  Then the rendered ServiceAccount, RoleBinding and Job (no ConfigMap when `has_files` is false)
    apply through @dir::install_obj into `instance.metadata.namespace`, then @wait::all blocks
    on the Job's completion up to `20*60` seconds, and @run returns `context` — which the
    install gate discards
  No mapped test.

Scenario: restore source rides through untouched
  Given `spec.initFrom` = secretName `peer-creds`, subPath `other-ns/peer`, snapshot `abcd1234`
  When @run renders
  Then the Job pod template carries `envFrom` secret `peer-creds`, `SUB_PATH` `other-ns/peer`
    and `RESTIC_SNAPSHOT` `abcd1234`, and the Pod later runs `agent service restore` against
    them — this file never inspects, validates or defaults any of the three
  And with all three absent the defaults apply (Secret `backup-settings`, own-namespace path,
    snapshot `()` per ./../lib/backup_context.sdd)

Scenario: existing init job is skipped and never awaited
  Given a `shop-init-restore` Job still present in the namespace from a failed earlier attempt
  When the rendered Job document reaches the dedup gate
  Then @list finds the name, `to_apply` is `false`, the Job is neither applied nor waited, and
    nothing is logged or marked; the ServiceAccount/RoleBinding still re-apply
  But given the probe itself raises
  Then the error is @log_warn'd and the Job is applied anyway

Tasks:
  [ ] Map the Scenarios to /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs (or a dedicated rhai_ file): today no
      test names this module; the mock engine would need vitals context, template fixtures and
      a mock Job list to pin the three scenarios.
  [?] A deduped existing Job is skipped silently and never awaited: a still-Running or failed
      previous init Job lets the install sail past init_from and stamp Ready with the restore
      possibly incomplete or dead. Decide whether to wait the existing job, fail, or at least
      log the skip.
  [?] The `20*60` @wait::all budget is hardcoded and shared by all four wait lanes: on a big
      volume the Elapsed raise writes the init-failed marker while the Job (backoffLimit 3) may
      still succeed afterwards. Decide on a configurable budget or a non-fatal wait.
  [?] `init_from_post` runs outside the try: its hook raise leaves the CR unmarked although the
      restore already finished. Decide whether to wrap it like the body or accept
      hook-author responsibility.
  [?] `init_from_pre`/`init_from_prepare`/`init_from_post` ship in no engine directory —
      package-side hook slots, same posture as ./install.sdd's unshipped hooks; confirm
      intentional.
  [?] The Job-probe @exist guard is dead defense for the built-in `"Job"` kind (exist == kind
      resolved at construction ≈ always true); simplify to list-only or document why the
      no-dedup fallback must exist.
  [?] `initFrom.version` is consumed on no part of this path (restore Pod re-uses the requested
      package as installed) — confirm the field's operator-side-only semantics.

Done when:
  Every Scenario carries a passing mock-engine test or a recorded decision, the render→apply→
    wait order and the single marker call still match the source, and `specdd lint` is green on
    this file.
